        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I&#39;m pretty sure I know the answer to this question, but it came up in a game tonight and I don&#39;t have it in my FAQ -- when do you pay the cost to use an ability in Tactics? &nbsp;I think it&#39;s really only important with abilities that cost a health to activate, like AZ&#39;s &quot;Thermal Shockwave&quot;. &nbsp;Must he lose the health, and only if he&#39;s still active have the ability go off, or does the ability go off, then he loses the health which could then incapacitate him?</p><p>If possible, I&#39;d love an official answer I can add to the FAQ.</p>",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 73,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 1,
        "deleted_at": null,
        "user_deleted": false,
        "edit_reason": null,
        "can_view_edit_history": true,
        "wiki": false,
        "can_accept_answer": false,
        "can_unaccept_answer": false,
        "accepted_answer": false,
        "topic_accepted_answer": false
      },
      {
        "id": 137725,
        "name": "lutherbellhendricksv",
        "username": "lutherbellhendricksv",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lutherbellhendricksv/{size}/2350_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-22T05:44:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You pay the cost upfront. If you pay your last health, you're incapacitated before the ability does anyone any good.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:14:08.623Z",
